      "description": "DMARC alignment is relaxed (adkim=r, aspf=r). Relaxed alignment accepts any subdomain of nic.in in the authenticated identifier.",
      "impact": "Relaxed alignment is the default and is appropriate for most senders. It does mean that anyone able to publish records under a subdomain can pass DMARC for the parent.",
      "remediation": "If every legitimate sender signs and sends as the exact domain, set adkim=s and aspf=s. If subdomains send mail, relaxed is the correct setting and no change is needed.",
